3. ETHICAL USE — MANDATORY CONDITION
   You MAY NOT use this Software, in whole or in part, to:

   (a) Conduct any security assessment, penetration test, vulnerability scan,
       exploitation, or security research on systems, networks, devices, or
       applications without explicit, documented, prior written authorization
       from the owner of the target systems.

   (b) Engage in any activity that violates applicable local, national, or
       international laws or regulations, including but not limited to the
       Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA), the Budapest Convention on
       Cybercrime, and equivalent laws in other jurisdictions.

   (c) Harm, stalk, harass, surveil, dox, or violate the privacy of any
       individual or group.

   (d) Develop or deploy offensive capabilities against critical infrastructure,
       healthcare systems, election systems, or emergency services.

   (e) Enable, support, or facilitate any criminal, terrorist, or state-sponsored
       malicious activity.

   (f) Circumvent, disable, or undermine security controls without explicit
       authorization from the affected system owner.

   Violation of this clause immediately and automatically terminates all rights
   granted under this License.

